\v 1 In¦317066 the¦317067 fifth¦317078 month¦317077 of¦317069 the¦317069 fourth¦317076 year of the¦317071 reign¦317069 of¦317071 Yehudah's¦317073 King¦317071 Tsidkiyah¦317070 \add !(Zedekiah¦317070)\add*,\x + \xo 28:1: \xt 2Ki 24:18-20; 2Ch 36:11-13.\x* Azzur's¦317084 son¦317082 Hananyah¦317081 who¦317086 was a ‘prophet¦317085’ from¦317087 Gibeon¦317087, said¦317079 to¦317080 me¦317080 in¦317088 Yahweh's¦317089 \add ≈temple¦317088\add* as priests¦317091 and¦317092 all¦317092 the¦317094 people¦317094 \add watched\add*, saying¦317095,
\v 2 “Yisrael's¦317103 god¦317102, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317100 says¦317099: I've¦317105 broken¦317105 the¦317108 yoke¦317108 of¦317108 the¦317109 Babylonian king¦317109.
\v 3 Within two¦317114 years¦317114, I¦317116, myself, will¦317117 bring¦317117 back¦317117 here all¦317124 the¦317126 utensils¦317126 from Yahweh's¦317128 residence that¦317129 the¦317133 Babylonian King¦317133 Nebuchadnezzar¦317131 got from¦317136 this place and¦317140 took¦317140 to Babylon¦317141.
\v 4 I, myself, will \add ≈also¦317143\add* bring¦317161 Yekonyah (\add Jeconiah,\add* the¦317146 son¦317146 of¦317146 Yehudah's King Yehoyakim¦317148/\add Jehoiakim\add*) back¦317161 to¦317162 this¦317165 place¦317164, and¦317152 all¦317154 the¦317156 exiles¦317156 from Yehudah¦317157 that¦317158 were taken to¦317159 Babylon¦317159, because¦317169 I'll¦317170 break¦317170 the¦317173 yoke¦317173 of¦317173 the¦317174 Babylonian king¦317174. That is Yahweh's¦317168 declaration¦317166.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦317177 the¦317179 prophet¦317179 Yirmeyah¦317178 spoke¦317177 to¦317180 the¦317183 prophet¦317183 Hananyah¦317182, as the¦317185 priests¦317185 and¦317186 all¦317187 the¦317189 people¦317189 standing¦317190 in¦317191 Yahweh's¦317192 \add ≈temple¦317191\add* \add ≈watched\add*,
\v 6 saying¦317194, “Let it¦317194 be so¦317198—may¦317199 Yahweh¦317200 do all that. May Yahweh¦317202 \add ≈confirm\add* your¦317205 messages¦317205 that¦317206 you¦317207 prophesied¦317207, to bring¦317208 the¦317209 \add ≈temple¦317210 utensils¦317209\add* back¦317208 to¦317217 this¦317220 place¦317219, along with all¦317213 the¦317215 exiles¦317215 from¦317216 Babylon¦317216.
\v 7 However¦317222, please¦317226 listen¦317224 to¦317224 this¦317228 message¦317227 that¦317229 I¦317230, myself, am¦317231 speaking¦317231 \add ≈as you and¦317233 all¦317234 the¦317236 people¦317236 listen\add*:
\v 8 The¦317238 prophets¦317238 who¦317239 \add ≈preceded\add* \add both\add* me and¦317242 you¦317242, prophesied¦317246 \add ≈long ago\add* that many¦317250 \add ≈nations¦317249\add* and¦317251 powerful¦317254 kingdoms¦317253 would experience \add #wars¦317255\add*, \add ≈terrible suffering\add*, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add*.
\v 9 The¦317259 prophet¦317259 who¦317260 prophesies¦317261 about¦317262 peace¦317262, \add &that\add* prophet¦317265 will¦317266 be¦317266 known¦317266 as ‘a truthful¦317272 prophet¦317267 sent¦317270 by Yahweh¦317271’ \add only\add* when¦317263 his message¦317264 comes¦317263 \add to pass\add*.”
\p
\v 10 Then¦317274 the prophet Hananyah¦317275 took¦317274 the¦317276 yoke bar off the prophet Yirmeyah's¦317282 neck¦317281, and¦317284 broke¦317284 it¦317284.
\v 11 Then¦317286 as all¦317289 the¦317291 people¦317291 watched, he said¦317292, “This is what Yahweh¦317295 says¦317294: Just like that, I'll¦317297 break¦317297 the¦317300 yoke¦317300 of¦317300 the¦317303 Babylonian King¦317303 Nebuchadnezzar¦317302 off the¦317311 neck¦317311 of¦317311 all¦317312 the¦317314 nations¦317314 within two¦317307 more years¦317307.”
\p Then¦317315 the prophet¦317317 Yirmeyah¦317316 \add ≈left¦317315 the¦317317 gathering\add*.
\p
\v 12 ⇔After¦317328 the prophet Hananyah¦317330 broke¦317329 the¦317331 yoke bar that had been on the prophet Yirmeyah's neck¦317336, Yahweh's¦317324 message¦317322 came to¦317325 Yirmeyah saying¦317339,
\v 13 “Go¦317341 and¦317342 tell¦317342 Hananyah¦317345 this: ‘Yahweh¦317349 says¦317348 that you've¦317352 broken¦317352 wooden¦317351 yoke bars, but in¦317354 their¦317354 place¦317354, you'll make¦317353 yoke bars out of¦317355 iron¦317356,’
\v 14 because¦317358 Yisrael's¦317365 god¦317364, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317362 says¦317361, ‘I've¦317368 put¦317368 an iron¦317367 yoke¦317366 bar on¦317369 the¦317371 neck¦317371 of¦317371 all¦317373 these¦317376 nations¦317375 to¦317377 serve¦317377 the¦317381 Babylonian King¦317381 Nebuchadnezzar¦317380, and¦317384 they¦317384 will¦317384 \add indeed\add* serve¦317384 him¦317384. I've¦317390 also¦317385 given¦317390 him the¦317388 animals¦317388 from the¦317389 countryside¦317389.’ ”
\p
\v 15 Then¦317393 the prophet Yirmeyah¦317394 told¦317393 the¦317395 prophet¦317395 Hananyah¦317398, “Listen¦317400, please¦317402, Hananyah¦317403. Yahweh¦317407 hasn't sent¦317406 you¦317406, and¦317408 you yourself have¦317409 made¦317409 this¦317413 people¦317412 \add group\add* \add ≈put their trust¦317409 in things that¦317413\add* \add ^aren't true\add*.
\v 16 Because¦317418 of that, Yahweh¦317421 says¦317420 this: ‘Listen, I'm¦317422 \add ≈removing you¦317423 from¦317424 this¦317427 world\add*. \add ≈You'll¦317428 die¦317429 this very\add* year¦317427, because¦317430 you¦317433 have¦317433 \add ≈said¦317433 things that would cause the people to rebel¦317432\add* against¦317434 Yahweh¦317436.’ ”
\p
\v 17 The¦317440 prophet¦317440 Hananyah¦317439 then¦317438 died¦317438 in¦317441 the¦317444 seventh¦317444 month¦317443 of that¦317442 year¦317441.
\c 29
\s1 Yirmeyah's letter to the exiled Jews
\rem /s1 Jeremiah's Letter to the Exiles in Babylon; Jeremiah's Letter to the Jews in Babylonia
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 The¦317453 prophet¦317453 Yirmeyah¦317452 sent¦317451 a \add ≈letter¦317449\add* from¦317454 Yerushalem¦317454 to¦317455 the¦317457 remainder¦317457 of¦317457 the¦317458 elders¦317458 of¦317458 the¦317459 exile¦317459, and¦317460 to¦317460 the¦317462 priests¦317462, and¦317463 to¦317463 the¦317465 prophets¦317465, and¦317466 to¦317466 all¦317468 the¦317470 people¦317470 that¦317471 Nebuchadnezzar¦317473 had¦317472 exiled¦317472 from¦317474 Yerushalem¦317474 to¦317475 Babylon¦317475\x + \xo 29:1-2: \xt 2Ki 24:12-16; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 2 after¦317477 the¦317481 \add ≈removal\add* from Yerushalem of King¦317481 Yekonyah \add !(Jeconiah)\add* and¦317482 the queen mother, the \add ≈court officials¦317484\add* and the leaders¦317484 of¦317484 Yehudah¦317485 and¦317486 Yerushalem¦317486, plus¦317487 the¦317487 \add #craftsmen¦317487\add* and¦317488 the¦317488 metalsmiths.
\v 3 \add He sent it\add* with Shafan's¦317495 son Elasah¦317492 and¦317496 Hilkiyah's¦317499 son Gemaryah¦317496, who¦317500 Yehudah's¦317505 King Tsidkiyah¦317502 \add !(Zedekiah)\add* sent¦317501 to¦317506 the¦317503 Babylonian King¦317503 Nebuchadnezzar¦317508 in Babylon. \add The letter\add* said¦317512,
\pi1
\v 4 Yisrael's¦317520 god¦317519, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317517 says¦317516 this to¦317521 all¦317521 \add ≈of you\add* that I've¦317526 exiled¦317526 from¦317527 Yerushalem¦317527 to¦317528 Babylon¦317528:
\v 5 Build¦317530 houses¦317531 and¦317532 live¦317532 in them, and¦317533 plant¦317533 gardens¦317534 and¦317535 eat¦317535 their¦317538 fruit.
\v 6 \add ≈Marry\add* and¦317542 \add ≈have children¦317543\add*. \add ≈Find\add* wives for¦317546 your sons and¦317548 give¦317551 your daughters \add ≈in marriage\add* so¦317553 that¦317553 they¦317553 \add also\add* \add ≈have children¦317554\add*. \add ≈Increase¦317556 in number\add* there¦317558—don't¦317559 become fewer.
\v 7 \add ≈In addition¦317563, the city¦317567 that I've¦317569 sent¦317569 you all into¦317569 exile¦317569 to¦317571, work to¦317571 make it more prosperous\add* and¦317572 pray¦317572 to¦317574 Yahweh¦317576 for it, because \add ≈if it prospers, its¦317578 prosperity will¦317579 belong¦317579 to¦317580 all of you¦317580\add*.
\v 8 That's because¦317584 Yisrael's¦317590 god¦317589, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317587 says¦317586 this: Don't¦317591 let¦317593 your¦317595 prophets¦317595 and¦317599 diviners¦317599 who¦317596 are¦317598 among¦317598 you deceive¦317593 you¦317594, and¦317600 don't¦317600 listen¦317602 to¦317603 your¦317605 dreams¦317605 that¦317606 you¦317607 \add wishfully\add* dream¦317608,
\v 9 because¦317610 \add @those¦317612 prophets¦317612\add* are¦317613 prophesying¦317613 \add ≈using\add* my¦317615 name¦317615 \add ≈but not¦317616 being truthful\add*—I¦317617 didn't send¦317617 them¦317617. That is Yahweh's¦317620 declaration¦317618.
\p
\v 10 “Because¦317623 this is what Yahweh¦317627 says¦317626: When seventy¦317632 years¦317633 \add ≈have passed\add* for¦317631 Babylon¦317631,\x + \xo 29:10: \xt 2Ch 36:21; Jer 25:11; Dan 9:2.\x* I'll¦317634 visit \add ≈take notice of you¦317635 all\add* \add again\add*, and¦317636 I'll¦317636 \add ≈implement¦317636\add* my¦317640 good¦317641 message¦317640 about¦317640 you—to bring¦317642 you all back¦317642 to¦317644 this place¦317646,
\v 11 because¦317649 I know¦317651 the¦317654 plans¦317654 that¦317655 I¦317656 \add ≈have\add* for you¦317658 all: plans¦317662 for peaceful well-being¦317663—not¦317664 to bring you¦317667 all harm¦317665, \add but rather\add* a¦317668 future¦317668 \add ≈with\add* hope¦317669. That is Yahweh's¦317661 declaration¦317659.
\v 12 Then¦317671 you'll¦317671 all call¦317671 out to me¦317672 \add for help\add*, and¦317673 you'll¦317673 come¦317673 and¦317674 pray¦317674 to¦317675 me¦317675, and¦317676 I'll¦317676 listen¦317676 to¦317677 you¦317677 all.
\v 13 You'll¦317679 search¦317679 for me¦317680, and¦317681 you'll¦317681 find¦317681 me¦317681, because¦317682 you'll¦317683 all¦317684 \add ≈want¦317683 to follow me¦317683 with complete sincerity\add*.\x + \xo 29:13: \xt Deu 4:29.\x*
\v 14 Then¦317688, Yahweh \add ≈has declared\add*, I'll¦317688 let¦317688 myself¦317688 be¦317688 found¦317688 by you¦317689 all, and¦317693 I'll¦317693 \add ≈bring you back¦317693 from\add* captivity¦317696. I'll¦317698 gather¦317698 you¦317699 all from¦317700 all¦317700 the¦317702 nations¦317702 and¦317703 all¦317703 the¦317705 places¦317705 that I¦317707 banished¦317707 you¦317708 to, and¦317713 I'll¦317713 bring¦317713 you all back to¦317715 the¦317717 place¦317717 that I¦317720 sent¦317720 you into¦317720 exile¦317720 from¦317722. That is Yahweh's declaration.
\pi1
\v 15 Because¦317724 you've¦317725 all said¦317725 that Yahweh¦317728 has¦317726 \add ≈appointed\add* prophets¦317729 for¦317727 \add %you¦317727\add* \add there\add* in Babylon¦317730,
\v 16 \add ≈then\add* Yahweh¦317738 \add ≈has something to say¦317737\add* about¦317739 the¦317741 king¦317741 sitting¦317742 on David's¦317746 throne¦317745 and¦317747 about all¦317749 the¦317751 people¦317751 living¦317752 in¦317753 this¦317754 city¦317753—your¦317755 relatives who¦317756 didn't¦317757 go¦317759 into¦317761 exile¦317761 with¦317760 you¦317760.
\v 17 So¦317763 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317765 says¦317764: Listen, I'm¦317767 about¦317768 to¦317768 send¦317768 \add ≈war\add*, famine¦317775 and \add ≈deadly diseases\add* against them. I'll¦317779 make¦317779 them¦317780 like¦317781 rotten¦317782 figs¦317781 that¦317783 are¦317786 so bad¦317787 they're \add ≈inedible\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Yes,\add* I'll¦317789 chase¦317789 after¦317790 them¦317790 with \add ≈war\add*, famine¦317792, and¦317793 \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, and¦317794 I'll¦317794 make¦317794 them¦317794 become a horror to¦317797 all¦317797 the¦317799 \add ≈world's¦317800\add* kingdoms¦317799—a¦317801 curse¦317801 and¦317802 a¦317802 desolation, and¦317803 a¦317803 reproach¦317804 and¦317804 \add ≈something to¦317804 be hissed¦317803 at\add* by all¦317805 the¦317807 nations¦317807 where¦317808 I've¦317810 driven¦317810 them¦317810,
\v 19 because¦317813 they¦317818 didn't listen¦317818 to¦317819 my¦317821 messages¦317821 that¦317825 I¦317826 sent¦317826 to¦317827 them¦317827 \add ≈over and over again\add* via my¦317830 servants¦317830 the¦317831 prophets¦317831, but all you¦317835 \add exiles\add* didn't listen¦317835. That is Yahweh's¦317838 declaration.
\p
\v 20 ⇔\add ≈But¦317840\add* all¦317845 you exiles¦317847 that I¦317850 sent¦317850 away from¦317851 Yerushalem¦317851 to¦317852 Babylon¦317852, listen¦317841 to Yahweh's¦317844 message¦317842:
\pi1
\v 21 Yisrael's¦317861 god¦317860, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317858, says¦317857 this about¦317880 Kolayah's¦317867 son Ahav¦317864 and¦317868 Maaseyah's¦317873 son Tsidkiyah¦317870, who¦317874 are¦317874 \add both\add* prophesying¦317874 untruths to¦317875 you¦317875 in¦317876 my¦317876 name¦317876: Listen, I'm¦317878 \add ≈handing¦317882 them over\add* to the¦317882 Babylonian King¦317884 Nebuchadnezzar¦317883, and¦317887 he'll¦317887 \add ≈kill¦317887 them¦317887 right in front of¦317888 you\add*.
\v 22 Then¦317890 because of them¦317891, a¦317892 \add new\add* curse¦317892 \add phrase\add* will be¦317890 taken¦317890 on by all¦317893 the¦317894 \add ≈Jewish\add* exiles¦317894 in¦317897 Babylon¦317897, which goes, “May¦317899 Yahweh¦317900 make¦317899 you¦317899 like¦317901 Tsidkiyah¦317901 and¦317902 Ahav¦317902, who¦317903 were roasted¦317905 in¦317909 the fire¦317909 by the Babylonian king¦317906,”
\v 23 because¦317911 they¦317913 did¦317913 something shameful¦317914 in¦317915 Yisrael¦317915 and¦317916 they¦317916 have committed¦317916 adultery¦317916 with the¦317919 wives¦317919 of¦317919 their¦317920 neighbours¦317920, and¦317921 they¦317921 spoke¦317921 untrue \add #messages¦317922\add* in¦317923 my¦317923 name¦317923 that¦317925 I¦317927 hadn't commanded¦317927 them¦317927 to. I¦317928 am the one \add ≈who knows that\add* and¦317933 I'm a¦317933 witness¦317933. That is Yahweh's¦317936 declaration¦317934.
\s1 Message to false prophet Shemayah
\rem /s1 A Message for Shemaiah; Message to Shemaiah; The Letter of Shemaiah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 24 \add Yahweh told me to\add* tell Shemayah¦317941 (the¦317942 Nehelamite¦317942) this:
\v 25 Yisrael's¦317952 god¦317951, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦317949 says¦317948 this: Because¦317954 you sent¦317957 letters¦317959 in¦317958 your¦317958 name¦317958 to¦317960 all¦317962 the¦317964 people¦317964 in¦317966 Yerushalem¦317966, and¦317967 to¦317967 the¦317973 priest¦317973 Tsefanyah¦317969 (Maaseyah's¦317972 son¦317970), and¦317974 to¦317974 all¦317975 the¦317977 priests¦317977, to¦317978 tell¦317978 \add <Tsefanyah\add*:
\pi1
\v 26 Yahweh¦317980 has¦317981 made¦317981 you¦317981, \add Tsefanyah,\add* priest¦317982 in¦317983 place¦317983 of¦317983 the¦317985 priest¦317985 Yehoyada¦317984 \add !(Jehoiada¦317984)\add*, to¦317986 be¦317986 \add #overseer¦317987\add* in Yahweh's¦317989 \add ≈temple¦317988\add* over every¦317990 man¦317992 who raves \add out loud\add*, making himself a prophet¦317994, and¦317995 you¦317995 must¦317995 put him¦317996 in¦317997 the¦317999 stocks¦317999 \add ≈with an iron¦318002 collar¦318002 around his\add* neck.
\v 27 \add ≈So¦318004 why\add* haven't you¦318007 rebuked¦318007 Yirmeyah¦318008 the¦318009 Antotite who's¦318010 prophesying¦318010 to¦318011 you¦318011 all,
\v 28 because¦318013 he's¦318017 sent¦318017 \add a letter\add* to¦318018 us¦318018 \add here\add* in Babylon¦318019 saying¦318020, “\add @Your exile\add* \add ≈will¦318021 last a long¦318021 time\add*. Build¦318023 houses¦318024 and¦318025 live¦318025 in them. Plant¦318026 gardens¦318027 and¦318028 eat¦318028 their¦318031 fruit.”
\p
\v 29 The¦318035 priest¦318035 Tsefanyah¦318034 read that¦318039 letter¦318038 to the¦318042 prophet¦318042 Yirmeyah¦318041,
\v 30 then¦318045 Yahweh¦318048 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦318046 to¦318049 Yirmeyah¦318051:
\v 31 Send¦318054 to¦318055 all¦318057 the¦318059 \add #exiles¦318059\add* to¦318060 tell¦318060 them: This is what Yahweh¦318063 says¦318062 about¦318064 Shemayah¦318066 the¦318067 Nehelamite¦318067: Because¦318068 Shemayah has¦318070 prophesied¦318070 to¦318071 you¦318071 all, \add ≈even though\add* I¦318073 didn't¦318074 send¦318075 him¦318075, and¦318076 he¦318076 made¦318076 you¦318077 trust¦318076 \add ^what's not true\add*,
\v 32 therefore Yahweh¦318086 says¦318085 this: Listen, I¦318087 \add ≈will punish¦318088\add* Shemayah¦318091 the¦318092 Nehelamite¦318092 and¦318093 \add ≈his descendants\add*. \add ≈None of his family\add* will¦318098 live¦318102 among this people, and¦318108 \add ≈he¦318110 won't experience the good¦318111 things\add* that¦318112 I'll¦318114 do¦318115 for¦318117 my¦318117 people, because¦318121 he's \add ≈encouraged\add* rebellion¦318123 against Yahweh. That is Yahweh's declaration¦318118.
\c 30
