\v 2 The¦324084 chief¦324084 bodyguard¦324086 took¦324083 Yirmeyah¦324087 \add aside\add* and¦324088 told¦324088 him¦324089, “Your¦324091 god¦324091 Yahweh¦324090 decreed this disaster¦324095 for this¦324096 place¦324099,
\v 3 then¦324102 he¦324102 caused¦324103 it to happen. Yahweh¦324104 did¦324103 just¦324105 as¦324105 he'd¦324106 decreed, since¦324107 you¦324109 \add >people\add* sinned¦324109 against \add *him¦324110\add* and¦324111 didn't¦324111 obey \add ≈him\add*. That's why \add all\add* this¦324119 has happened to you¦324116 people.
\v 4 \add ≈But¦324121\add* now¦324121 listen, I've¦324123 released¦324123 you¦324123 today from¦324125 your chains¦324127. If¦324132 \add ≈you choose\add* to¦324136 come¦324136 with¦324137 me¦324137 to Babylon¦324138, I'll¦324140 \add ≈look after\add* you¦324144, \add ≈but¦324145 if¦324145 you\add* \add ^don't want to\add*, then look¦324154 \add ≈around\add* and¦324162 go \add ≈wherever you think best\add*.
