\v 7 \add ≈Now some¦324260\add* commanders¦324234 of¦324234 \add Judean\add* \add ≈soldiers\add* who were still in¦324237 the¦324237 countryside¦324237, along with their¦324239 men heard¦324231 that¦324240 the¦324243 Babylonian king¦324243 had¦324242 made Ahikam's¦324251 son¦324249 Gedalyah¦324248 governor over the¦324252 land¦324252.\x + \xo 40:7-9: \xt 2Ki 25:22-24.\x* \add ≡They also heard\add* that he'd¦324255 \add ≈put him¦324256 in charge of\add* the men¦324257, women¦324258, and children who were the¦324260 poorest¦324260 people¦324260 in the¦324261 land¦324261—those¦324262 who¦324262 hadn't been¦324265 exiled¦324265 to¦324266 Babylon¦324266.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦324268\add* they¦324268 went¦324268 to¦324269 Gedalyah¦324271 at Mitspah¦324272. Those \add ≈who went\add* were Netanyah's¦324276 son Yishmael¦324273, Kareah's¦324281 sons¦324274 Yohanan¦324277 and¦324278 Yonatan¦324278, Tanhumet's¦324285 son¦324279 Serayah¦324282, the¦324286 sons¦324286 of¦324288 Ofai the¦324290 Netofatite, and¦324291 Maakati's¦324294 son Yezanyah¦324291, and¦324296 their¦324296 men¦324296.
\v 9 Gedalyah¦324300 (son¦324301 of¦324301 Ahikam¦324303, son¦324304 of¦324304 Shafan¦324306) \add made a promise\add* to them and their¦324307 men¦324307, saying¦324308, “Don't¦324309 be¦324311 afraid¦324311 to serve¦324312 the¦324313 \add ≈Babylonian\add* officials. Live¦324314 in¦324315 the¦324315 land¦324315 and¦324316 serve¦324316 the¦324319 Babylonian king¦324319, and it¦324321 will go¦324321 well¦324321 with you¦324322.
\v 10 See, I'm living¦324326 in Mitspah¦324327 to meet with the \add ≈Babylonians\add* who¦324331 came¦324332 to¦324333 us¦324333. \add ≈So¦324334\add* harvest wine¦324336, summer¦324337 fruit¦324337, and¦324338 oil¦324338 and¦324339 store them¦324339 in¦324340 your¦324340 containers¦324340. Live¦324341 in¦324342 the cities¦324342 that¦324343 you've¦324345 \add ≈occupied¦324345\add*.”
\v 11 Then¦324347 all¦324348 the¦324350 Judeans¦324350 in¦324353 Moav¦324353, among¦324355 the¦324355 people¦324355 of¦324355 Ammon¦324357, and¦324358 in¦324358 Edom¦324358, and¦324359 in¦324360 every¦324360 land¦324362 heard¦324363 that¦324364 the¦324367 Babylonian king¦324367 had¦324366 allowed a¦324370 \add ≈small number of people\add* to¦324371 stay in Yehudah¦324371, and¦324372 that he'd¦324373 appointed¦324373 Gedalyah¦324377 (son¦324378 of¦324378 Ahikam¦324380, son¦324381 of¦324381 Shafan¦324383) over¦324374 them¦324374.
