\v 6 \add That included\add* men¦325619 and¦325620 women¦325622, children, the king's daughters¦325628, and¦325630 all¦325631 the¦325633 people that Nevuzar-Adan, the¦325637 king's chief¦325637 bodyguard¦325639 Nevuzar-Adan had¦325635 left¦325635 with¦325640 Gedalyah¦325642 (son¦325643 of¦325643 Ahikam¦325645, son¦325646 of¦325646 Shafan¦325648), and¦325649 including the¦325651 prophet¦325651 Yirmeyah¦325650 and¦325652 Neriyah's¦325657 son Baruk¦325654.
\v 7 Then¦325659 they¦325659 went¦325659 to Egypt¦325661 because¦325662 they¦325664 \add ≈took no notice of¦325665 Yahweh's¦325666 instructions\add* and¦325667 they¦325667 arrived¦325667 at Tahpanhes¦325670.
\p
\v 8 In¦325680 Tahpanhes¦325680, Yahweh¦325676 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦325679 a message¦325674:
\v 9 \add ≈Get¦325683\add* some large¦325686 stones¦325685 and¦325687 \add ≈while the people¦325697 from Yehudah are watching\add*, \add ≈push\add* them¦325687 into¦325688 the mortar¦325688 in¦325689 the pavement at¦325691 the¦325691 entrance¦325691 to Far-oh's \add !(Pharaoh's)\add* \add ≈palace¦325692\add* at Tahpanhes¦325695.
\v 10 Then¦325700 tell¦325700 \add @the¦325701 Judeans¦325701\add* that¦325724 Yisrael's¦325708 god¦325707, Commander-in-chief says¦325704: Listen, I'm¦325709 about¦325710 to¦325710 send¦325710 messengers¦325706 to my¦325718 servant¦325718 the¦325715 Babylonian King¦325715 Nebuchadnezzar¦325714, to summon him \add here\add*. I'll¦325719 place¦325719 his¦325720 throne¦325720 over the top of those¦325723 hidden¦325725 stones¦325722, and¦325726 he'll¦325726 spread¦325726 his \add ≈royal\add* tent¦325729 over¦325731 them¦325731.
\v 11 He'll¦325733 come¦325733 here to attack¦325735 Egypt¦325739 \add ≈and he'll¦325735 kill those¦325740 that¦325740 I've assigned to¦325742 die¦325742, and¦325743 similarly for¦325744 those to¦325745 be¦325747 taken captive or run through with a\add* sword.
\v 12 Then¦325750 \add ?≈he'll¦325756\add* light¦325750 a fire¦325751 in¦325752 the¦325752 temples¦325752 of¦325752 Egypt's¦325754 gods¦325753. \add @Nebuchadnezzar¦325755\add* will¦325755 \add either\add* burn¦325755 them¦325755 or \add ≈carry¦325756 them¦325756 away\add*. He'll¦325757 clean Egypt¦325761 out just¦325762 like¦325762 shepherds¦325765 pick lice off their clothes¦325768, and¦325769 then he'll¦325769 \add ≈quietly\add* leave¦325769
\v 13 \add after\add* smashing¦325773 the¦325776 \add stone\add* pillars¦325776 at \add ≈Heliopolis\add* and¦325782 burning¦325788 the¦325784 temples¦325784 of¦325784 Egypt's¦325787 gods¦325785.
\c 44
\s1 Yahweh's message to the Judeans in Egypt
\rem /s1 Denunciation of Persistent Idolatry; The Lord's Message to the Israelites in Egypt; Disaster Because of Idolatry; Judgment for Idolatry
\p
\v 1 Yahweh spoke to¦325795 Yirmeyah¦325797 about¦325798 all¦325799 the¦325801 Judeans¦325801 who lived in¦325806 Migdol¦325806, Tahpanhes¦325807, and¦325808 Memphis¦325808 in \add northern/lower\add* Egypt¦325804, as well as those in¦325809 Patros¦325810 \add in southern/upper Egypt\add*:
\v 2 Yisrael's¦325820 god¦325819, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325817 says¦325816 that you yourselves have¦325822 seen¦325822 all¦325824 the¦325826 disasters¦325826 that¦325827 I¦325828 \add ≈sent to\add* Yerushalem¦325831 and¦325832 Yehudah's¦325836 other cities¦325835. See, they're¦325837 \add just\add* \add #ruins¦325838\add* \add ≈today without anyone living¦325843 in¦325842\add* them¦325842.
\v 3 \add ≈That's because\add* of¦325845 the \add ≈wicked¦325846\add* things they¦325848 did¦325848 to¦325849 provoke¦325849 me¦325849 to¦325849 anger¦325849 by going¦325850 to¦325851 burn incense and to¦325852 worship¦325852 other¦325854 gods¦325853 that¦325855 neither they themselves, nor you¦325859, nor your¦325860 ancestors¦325860 had \add ≈ever heard about¦325860 before\add*.
\v 4 I¦325862 repeatedly sent¦325862 all¦325866 my¦325868 servants¦325868, the¦325869 prophets¦325869, to them to tell¦325872 \add >the people\add* to stop doing those \add ≈detestable¦325880\add* \add #things¦325878\add* that¦325882 I¦325883 hate¦325883,
\v 5 \add ≈but¦325885\add* they¦325886 didn't listen¦325886. They¦325889 \add ≈refused to take any notice of¦325892 it, or to stop their wicked¦325894 activities like burning incense¦325896\add* to¦325897 other¦325898 gods¦325897.
\v 6 \add ≈So\add* my¦325901 anger¦325902 and¦325900 rage¦325901 was poured¦325900 out¦325900 and¦325903 burnt¦325903 in¦325904 Yehudah's¦325905 cities¦325904 and¦325906 Yerushalem's¦325907 streets¦325906 \add like a fire\add* and¦325908 they're¦325908 \add still\add* \add ≈desolate¦325910\add* \add #ruins¦325909\add* to¦325910 this¦325912 day¦325911.
